CRYSTAL UNIT-CELL
============================================================

------------------------------------------------------------
0. LEGEND
------------------------------------------------------------
Axes:
  x = e1
  y = e2   (conventional monoclinic unique axis)
  z = e3

Length markers:
  (=)   equal length
  (≠)   distinct length

Angle markers:
  +     right angle (90°)
  / \   oblique angle (≠ 90°)
 120°   explicit hexagonal basal angle

RDG Triad:
  S = Structure (length relations)
  I = Interaction (angle relations)
  D = Dynamics (symmetry operators)

------------------------------------------------------------
1. CUBIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| = |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C4x, C4y, C4z

ASCII:
        z
        |
        |
        +------ y
       /
      x

------------------------------------------------------------
2. TETRAGONAL
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C4z

        z (≠)
        |
        |
        +------ y (=)
       /
      x (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
3. ORTHORHOMBIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C2x, C2y, C2z

        z (≠)
        |
        |
        +------ y (≠)
       /
      x (≠)

------------------------------------------------------------
4. HEXAGONAL
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: ∠(e1,e2)=120°, ∠(e1,e3)=90°, ∠(e2,e3)=90°
D: C6z

  - Hexagonal basal plane angle (x,y) = 120° is correctly shown.

ASCII:
        z (≠)
        |
        |
       / 120°
      x (=)
       \
        y (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
5. TRIGONAL (RHOMBOHEDRAL)
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| = |e3|
I: α = β = γ ≠ 90°
D: C3

  - All three edges equal.
  - All three angles equal and oblique (α=β=γ≠90°).

        z (=)
       /
      /  α
     x (=)
      \
       y (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
6. MONOCLINIC (UNIQUE AXIS b = y)
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: ∠(x,y)=90°, ∠(y,z)=90°, ∠(x,z)=β≠90°
D: C2y or σ

  - Conventional unique axis is b = y.
  - Single oblique angle is β = ∠(x,z).

        z (≠)
        \
         \  β
          x (≠)

        +------ y (≠)

------------------------------------------------------------
7. TRICLINIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: α ≠ β ≠ γ, all ≠ 90°
D: none

  - All lengths distinct.
  - All angles distinct and non-orthogonal.

        z (≠)
        \
         \  γ
          x (≠)
           \
            \  α
             y (≠)

------------------------------------------------------------
8. COMPACT OPERATOR TABLE
------------------------------------------------------------
CRYSTAL_SYSTEM := {
  cubic:       {S:{e1=e2=e3},     I:{90,90,90},     D:{C4x,C4y,C4z}},
  tetragonal:  {S:{e1=e2≠e3},     I:{90,90,90},     D:{C4z}},
  orthorhombic:{S:{e1≠e2≠e3},     I:{90,90,90},     D:{C2x,C2y,C2z}},
  hexagonal:   {S:{e1=e2≠e3},     I:{120,90,90},    D:{C6z}},
  trigonal:    {S:{e1=e2=e3},     I:{α,α,α},        D:{C3}},
  monoclinic:  {S:{e1≠e2≠e3},     I:{β},            D:{C2y|σ}},
  triclinic:   {S:{e1≠e2≠e3},     I:{α≠β≠γ},        D:{∅}}
}

